description:
## What

Implement the **Organization-validated** S/MIME tier as a Profile type in `pkix-profiles-cabf`. Per CA/B Forum S/MIME BR §7.6.1 and §8: this tier proves the mailbox AND verified ownership of the organization domain. Distinct from Mailbox-validated (the current `SmimeProfile`) in subject DN field requirements, allowed SAN content, and asserted policy OID.

## API shape

Per the spec-taxonomy principle (PKIX-mzsk) and the wrapper-set decision (PKIX-fmtv.7, option C2: Profile is a generic parameter), file as a distinct Profile type:

```rust
/// Organization-validated S/MIME BR subscriber-certificate profile.
///
/// Reference, not authoritative. CA/B Forum S/MIME Baseline Requirements
/// v1.0.14 (or whichever revision the cabf workspace has refreshed to).
/// Section §7.6.1 (Organization-validated profile) + §8 (validation rules).
///
/// Asserts policy OID `2.23.140.1.5.2.1` (Organization-validated).
///
/// Required Subject DN fields per BR: organizationName, optionally
/// jurisdictionCountry/State/Locality, organizationIdentifier.
/// Subject SAN: rfc822Name (one or more); X.500 dirName when present
/// must match Subject DN.
pub struct SmimeOrganizationValidated;

impl Profile for SmimeOrganizationValidated {
    fn policy(&self, now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy {
        // - required_leaf_eku: id-kp-emailProtection
        // - require_rfc822_san: true
        // - max_validity: per BR §6.3.2 (same cap as other S/MIME tiers)
        // - required_policy_oids: [2.23.140.1.5.2.1]  // Organization-validated
        // - required_subject_dn_attributes: [organizationName]
        // ... other tier-specific predicates
    }
    fn version(&self) -> &'static str { "1.0.14" }  // matches PKIX-d5rh dotted-version convention
}

pub const fn smime_org_policy(now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy {
    SmimeOrganizationValidated.policy(now_unix)
}
```

## Test fixtures

Per Mark's 2026-05-11 decision (option d, recorded in PKIX-jbvb notes): pull from BOTH zlint testdata/ AND pkilint fixtures. Cross-validation between the two dominant ecosystem interpretations.

- zlint: `~/GIT/zlint/v3/lints/cabf_smime/*/testdata/` (Apache-2.0, attributable, cite per-fixture)
- pkilint: `~/GIT/pkilint/tests/integration_certificates/cabf/smime/` (Apache-2.0, attributable)

For Organization-validated specifically:
- Positive cases: certs that zlint AND pkilint both classify as Organization-validated and accept
- Negative cases: certs from other tiers (Mailbox, Sponsor, Individual) that should be rejected when `SmimeOrganizationValidated` is the active Profile

Record fixture provenance per-cert in `pkix-profiles-cabf/tests/fixtures/smime_org/SOURCES.md` or equivalent.

## Acceptance

- [ ] `pkix_profiles_cabf::SmimeOrganizationValidated` ships and impls `Profile`
- [ ] `smime_org_policy(now_unix)` free function alias exists
- [ ] Reference-not-authoritative rustdoc disclaimer header matches existing `pkix-profiles-cabf` types
- [ ] Rustdoc cites CA/B Forum S/MIME BR v1.0.14 + §7.6.1 + §8 (or whichever section numbers actually contain the Organization-validated profile after PKIX-d5rh's citation refresh lands)
- [ ] At least 2 positive + 2 negative test fixtures per the dual-oracle convention, with provenance recorded
- [ ] Tests pass against both fixture sources
- [ ] CHANGELOG entry in `pkix-profiles-cabf`
- [ ] `pkix-profiles-cabf` rustdoc top-level updated to enumerate the new type alongside `SmimeProfile`

## Out of scope

- Renaming the current `SmimeProfile` to `SmimeMailboxValidated` for naming parity — could be a follow-up bead if the type-rename signal-to-noise is worth it; not blocking for this bead
- Sponsor-validated (PKIX-jbvb.2)
- Individual-validated (PKIX-jbvb.3)
- Composing tiers into a "any of these tiers" enforcement (caller-side concern)

## Blocks on

- PKIX-mzsk (AGENTS.md amendment) — for principled justification
- PKIX-d5rh (CABF citation refresh) — to align section numbers with current BR layout before this bead's rustdoc cites them

